where slug = 'the-new-covenant'
  and study_series_id = 'e4000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000007a';

-- The Law of Love — Lesson 6: The Law of Liberty (guided reader JSON).
delete from public.lesson_sections
where lesson_id = 'd3000007-0000-4000-8000-000000000899';

update public.lessons
set reader_content = $tlol_l6_reader$
{"openingThought":"Most people do not connect law with freedom.\n\nThey hear \"law\" and think restriction.\n\nBut Scripture uses a different phrase:\n\n\"The law of liberty.\"\n\nThat sounds strange until we understand what God's law really is.\n\nGod's law does not protect selfishness.\n\nIt protects love.\n\nIt protects worship.\nIt protects truth.\nIt protects marriage.\nIt protects life.\nIt protects trust.\nIt protects human dignity.\n\nSin promises freedom but produces bondage.\n\nGod's law reveals the kind of life where love can actually breathe.","scriptureRef":"James 1:25","scriptureQuote":"But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.","scriptureAfterPrimary":"James calls God's law the perfect law of liberty.\n\nThat means God's law is not the enemy of freedom.\n\nIt shows what freedom looks like when love is restored.\n\nTrue freedom is not doing whatever desire demands.\n\nTrue freedom is being able to live in harmony with God's love.","scriptureSecondaryRef":"Psalm 119:32","scriptureSecondaryQuote":"I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart.","scriptureAfterSecondary":"The psalmist does not see God's commandments as a prison.\n\nHe sees them as a path he can run with joy when God enlarges the heart.\n\nGod's law and true freedom belong together.","scriptureSupplementBlocks":[{"type":"scripture","reference":"Romans 13:10","quote":"Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"John 8:36","quote":"If the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed."}],"teachingPoints":["1. God's law is called the law of liberty\n\nJames calls God's law the perfect law of liberty.\n\nThat means God's law is not the enemy of freedom.\n\nIt shows what freedom looks like when love is restored.\n\nTrue freedom is not doing whatever desire demands.\n\nTrue freedom is being able to live in harmony with God's love.","2. Sin promises freedom but creates bondage\n\nSin often feels like freedom at first.\n\nDo what you want.\nSay what you want.\nTake what you want.\nWorship what you want.\n\nBut selfishness does not produce liberty.\n\nIt produces slavery to appetite, pride, fear, lust, anger, comparison, and guilt.\n\nGod's law protects us from the bondage sin creates.","3. Love does no harm\n\nRomans says love works no harm to a neighbor.\n\nThat is why love fulfills the law.\n\nThe commandments are not random barriers.\n\nThey are boundaries that protect life and relationship.\n\nA world without truth, faithfulness, worship, contentment, and respect is not free.\n\nIt is broken.","4. Jesus makes freedom real\n\nJohn 8 says the Son makes us free indeed.\n\nThe law can describe freedom, but Jesus gives the power to live in it.\n\nHe frees us from condemnation.\n\nHe frees us from sin's mastery.\n\nHe frees us to love God and others from a renewed heart."],"wordStudyBeforeStudyInsight":true,"wordStudyStepTitle":"Word Insight","wordStudyStepIntro":"","wordStudy":{"surface":"Liberty","lemma":"ἐλευθερία","transliteration":"eleutheria","meaning":"Freedom, release from bondage, and the ability to live as God designed.","strongs":"G1657","reference":"James 1:25","note":"Biblical liberty is not lawlessness.\n\nIt is freedom from the slavery of sin so we can live in love.\n\nGod's law is called the law of liberty because it describes the life Jesus frees us to live."},"studyInsight":{"title":"Study Insight","placement":"after_teaching","variant":"christ_connection","body":"Freedom without love becomes destruction.\n\nThat is why God's law matters.\n\nIf someone says, \"I am free to lie,\" trust dies.\n\nIf someone says, \"I am free to steal,\" safety dies.\n\nIf someone says, \"I am free to betray,\" covenant dies.\n\nIf someone says, \"I am free to worship anything,\" the heart becomes enslaved to idols.\n\nGod's commandments are not chains on love.\n\nThey are the shape of love.\n\nThe more Christ restores the heart, the more God's law begins to look less like pressure and more like freedom."},"studyInsightBlocks":[{"type":"studyVisual","title":"Two kinds of freedom","accent":"sage","payload":{"variant":"comparison","leftTitle":"False Freedom","rightTitle":"True Freedom","leftItems":["do whatever self wants","bondage","harm","guilt","broken trust"],"rightItems":["live in God's love","peace","trust","worship","restored relationships"]},"footnote":"The law of liberty protects the life love was made for."},{"type":"scriptureChain","title":"The Law of Liberty","references":[{"reference":"James 1:25"},{"reference":"Psalm 119:32"},{"reference":"Romans 13:10"},{"reference":"John 8:36"}]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Takeaway: God's law is not bondage. It reveals the life of love and freedom that Jesus restores in us."}],"reflectPrompt":"Where have you mistaken freedom for doing whatever you want?\n\nThink about a place where God's boundary may actually be protecting your peace, relationships, worship, or future.","lifeApplicationStepTitle":"Life Application and Prayer","lifeApplication":"This week, look at one commandment through the lens of freedom.\n\nAsk:\n\n\"What bondage does this command protect me from?\"\n\nFor example:\n\nTruthfulness protects me from deception and broken trust.\n\nFaithfulness protects me from betrayal and divided love.\n\nSabbath rest protects me from endless striving.\n\nWorship protects me from idols that cannot save.\n\nDo not just ask, \"What is God stopping me from doing?\"\n\nAsk, \"What kind of freedom is God inviting me into?\"\n\nPrayer:\n\nFather, help me see Your law as the law of liberty. Free me from false ideas of freedom that lead to bondage. Teach me to love what protects life, truth, worship, and relationship. Let Jesus make me free indeed, and help me walk in Your commandments with a heart enlarged by grace. Amen.","prayer":"","completionSummary":"God's law is the law of liberty. It does not chain love down. It shows the free, whole, restored life Jesus came to give.","lessonQuiz":{"eyebrow":"CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING","title":"Quick Review","description":"Check your understanding before moving on.","settings":{"quizRequired":false,"passingScore":70,"allowRetake":true},"questions":[{"id":"tlol-l6-q1","prompt":"What does James 1:25 call God's law?","options":["The perfect law of liberty","The law of confusion","The law of fear","The law of bondage"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"James calls God's law the perfect law of liberty, showing that God's law is connected to true freedom."},{"id":"tlol-l6-q2","prompt":"According to Romans 13:10, what does love do?","options":["Works no harm to a neighbor","Ignores truth","Encourages selfishness","Destroys faithfulness"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Romans says love works no harm to a neighbor, therefore love fulfills the law."},{"id":"tlol-l6-q3","prompt":"According to John 8:36, who makes us free indeed?","options":["The Son","Human pride","Selfish desire","Fear"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Jesus said if the Son makes you free, you shall be free indeed."},{"id":"tlol-l6-q4","prompt":"What is true freedom according to this lesson?","options":["Living in harmony with God's love","Doing whatever desire demands","Ignoring every boundary","Rejecting relationship with God"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"True freedom is not lawlessness. It is freedom from sin's bondage so we can live in God's love."},{"id":"tlol-l6-q5","kind":"reflection","prompt":"Which commandment can you now see as protection instead of restriction?","explanation":"God's law protects the life love was made for. His boundaries guard worship, trust, relationships, and freedom."}]}}
$tlol_l6_reader$::jsonb
where slug = 'the-law-of-liberty'
  and study_series_id = 'e4000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000007a';

-- The Law of Love — Lesson 7: Living a Life of Love (guided reader JSON).
delete from public.lesson_sections
where lesson_id = 'd3000007-0000-4000-8000-000000000900';

update public.lessons
set reader_content = $tlol_l7_reader$
{"openingThought":"The goal of God's law is not religious performance.\n\nThe goal is love.\n\nNot love as a slogan.\nNot love as a feeling only.\nNot love as approval of everything.\n\nReal love.\n\nLove that honors God.\nLove that tells the truth.\nLove that protects trust.\nLove that serves.\nLove that refuses to harm.\nLove that reflects the heart of Jesus.\n\nThe Christian life is not about earning God's love.\n\nIt is about receiving His love so deeply that it begins to flow through us.\n\nWe love because He first loved us.","scriptureRef":"1 John 4:19","scriptureQuote":"We love him, because he first loved us.","scriptureAfterPrimary":"That order matters.\n\nChristian love does not begin with human effort.\n\nIt begins with receiving God's love in Christ.\n\nGod's love becomes the source, motive, and pattern for how we live.","scriptureSecondaryRef":"John 13:34-35","scriptureSecondaryQuote":"A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another. By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another.","scriptureAfterSecondary":"Christ is the standard.\n\nNot culture.\nNot emotions.\nNot convenience.\nNot personal preference.\n\nJesus shows us love that serves, forgives, sacrifices, tells the truth, and seeks the good of others.","scriptureSupplementBlocks":[{"type":"scripture","reference":"Galatians 5:13-14","quote":"For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another. For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"Romans 13:10","quote":"Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law."}],"teachingPoints":["1. Love begins with God\n\nFirst John says we love because God first loved us.\n\nThat order matters.\n\nChristian love does not begin with human effort.\n\nIt begins with receiving God's love in Christ.\n\nGod's love becomes the source, motive, and pattern for how we live.","2. Jesus shows the shape of love\n\nJesus said, \"Love one another; as I have loved you.\"\n\nThat means Christ is the standard.\n\nNot culture.\nNot emotions.\nNot convenience.\nNot personal preference.\n\nJesus shows us love that serves, forgives, sacrifices, tells the truth, and seeks the good of others.","3. Love serves instead of using people\n\nGalatians says, \"By love serve one another.\"\n\nSin uses people.\n\nLove serves people.\n\nSin asks, \"What can I get?\"\n\nLove asks, \"How can I bless?\"\n\nA life shaped by God's law is not self-centered. It becomes others-centered because grace has changed the heart.","4. Love fulfills the law\n\nRomans and Galatians both connect love with the fulfillment of the law.\n\nThis does not mean love makes God's commandments meaningless.\n\nIt means love is what the commandments were describing all along.\n\nThe law points to love.\n\nGrace restores love.\n\nThe Spirit produces love."],"wordStudyBeforeStudyInsight":true,"wordStudyStepTitle":"Word Insight","wordStudyStepIntro":"","wordStudy":{"surface":"Fulfill","lemma":"πληρόω","transliteration":"plēroō","meaning":"To bring to fullness, complete, or live out the intended purpose.","strongs":"G4137","reference":"Romans 13:10","note":"Love fulfills the law because love is the purpose the law was always pointing toward.\n\nGod's commandments are not empty rules.\n\nThey describe a life where love for God and love for others becomes real."},"studyInsight":{"title":"Study Insight","placement":"after_teaching","variant":"christ_connection","body":"The Law of Love has shown one clear truth:\n\nGod's law is not opposed to love.\n\nGod's law reveals love.\n\nBut fallen human beings cannot produce that love on their own.\n\nThat is why we need Jesus.\n\nHe gives righteousness as a gift.\nHe writes the law in the heart.\nHe frees us from sin's bondage.\nHe teaches us to live by the Spirit.\nHe forms love within us.\n\nSo the Christian life is not:\n\n\"Keep the law so God will love you.\"\n\nIt is:\n\n\"Receive God's love in Christ, then let His love shape your life.\"\n\nThat changes everything.\n\nObedience becomes response, not performance.\n\nService becomes gratitude, not self-promotion.\n\nLove becomes the evidence that Christ is working in us."},"studyInsightBlocks":[{"type":"studyVisual","title":"The Law of Love","accent":"sage","payload":{"variant":"sequence","steps":[{"label":"God is love","subtitle":""},{"label":"His law reveals love","subtitle":""},{"label":"Sin bends us away from love","subtitle":""},{"label":"Jesus gives righteousness","subtitle":""},{"label":"The Spirit writes love within","subtitle":""},{"label":"God's law becomes liberty","subtitle":""},{"label":"Believers live love in action","subtitle":""}]},"footnote":"We do not obey to become loved. We obey because love has reached us."},{"type":"scriptureChain","title":"Love Lived Out","references":[{"reference":"1 John 4:19"},{"reference":"John 13:34-35"},{"reference":"Galatians 5:13-14"},{"reference":"Romans 13:10"}]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Takeaway: God's love comes first. As we receive His love in Christ, we begin to live love toward God and others."}],"reflectPrompt":"Where is God inviting you to live love more clearly right now?\n\nThink about your home, friendships, church, workplace, private life, online behavior, or the way you treat people who frustrate you.","lifeApplicationStepTitle":"Life Application and Prayer","lifeApplication":"This week, practice love in action.\n\nChoose one person and ask:\n\n\"What would love look like here?\"\n\nThen make it practical.\n\nTell the truth kindly.\nServe without needing credit.\nForgive instead of rehearsing the offense.\nListen before defending yourself.\nHonor God when no one sees.\nRefuse to harm someone with your words.\n\nDo not make love vague.\n\nMake it visible.\n\nPrayer:\n\nFather, thank You for loving me first. Thank You for showing me Your heart through Jesus. Write Your law of love deeper into my heart. Teach me to love You with all that I am and to love others with humility, truth, patience, and grace. Let my life show that Your love is real. Amen.","prayer":"","completionSummary":"You have completed The Law of Love. God's law reveals His character, exposes our need, points us to Jesus, and shows the life of love He writes in the heart through grace.","seriesCompleteScreen":{"title":"Study Complete","message":"You have completed The Law of Love. God's law reveals His character, exposes our need, points us to Jesus, and shows the life of love He writes in the heart through grace.","primaryCta":{"label":"Back to Foundations Path","href":"/paths/foundations"},"secondaryCta":{"label":"Review this study","href":"/study-library/the-law-of-love"}},"lessonQuiz":{"eyebrow":"CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING","title":"Quick Review","description":"Check your understanding before moving on.","settings":{"quizRequired":false,"passingScore":70,"allowRetake":true},"questions":[{"id":"tlol-l7-q1","prompt":"According to 1 John 4:19, why do we love God?","options":["Because He first loved us","Because we earned His love","Because fear saves us","Because love is unnecessary"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"First John says we love Him because He first loved us. God's love comes before our response."},{"id":"tlol-l7-q2","prompt":"According to John 13:34-35, how will people know Jesus' disciples?","options":["By their love for one another","By their wealth","By their popularity","By their arguments"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Jesus said people would know His disciples by their love for one another."},{"id":"tlol-l7-q3","prompt":"According to Galatians 5:13, how should believers serve one another?","options":["By love","By pride","By force","By selfish ambition"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Galatians says believers are to serve one another by love."},{"id":"tlol-l7-q4","prompt":"According to Romans 13:10, what fulfills the law?","options":["Love","Fear","Control","Selfishness"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Romans says love does no harm to a neighbor, therefore love is the fulfilling of the law."},{"id":"tlol-l7-q5","kind":"reflection","prompt":"What is one practical way you can make love visible this week?","explanation":"Biblical love is not only a feeling. It becomes action that reflects the heart of God."}]}}
$tlol_l7_reader$::jsonb
where slug = 'living-a-life-of-love'
  and study_series_id = 'e4000001-0000-4000-8000-00000000007a';

-- Made New in Christ — Lesson 1: Good News, Not Good Advice (guided reader JSON).
delete from public.lesson_sections
where lesson_id = 'd3000007-0000-4000-8000-000000000887';

update public.lessons
set reader_content = $mnic_l1_reader$
{"openingThought":"Most people think Christianity starts with advice.\n\nTry harder.\nDo better.\nFix yourself.\nStop failing.\nBecome worthy.\n\nBut the gospel does not begin with what you must do.\n\nIt begins with what Jesus has already done.\n\nThat is what makes the gospel good news.\n\nAdvice tells you what still needs to happen.\n\nNews tells you what has already happened.\n\nThe gospel announces that Christ died for our sins, rose again, and opened the way for us to receive salvation by faith.\n\nRight living matters.\n\nBut right living is not the root of salvation.\n\nIt is the fruit of receiving Christ.","scriptureRef":"1 Corinthians 15:3","scriptureQuote":"For I delivered unto you first of all that which I also received, how that Christ died for our sins according to the scriptures.","scriptureAfterPrimary":"Paul begins with what Jesus has done, not what we must accomplish.\n\nChrist died for our sins according to the scriptures.","scriptureSecondaryRef":"1 Corinthians 15:4","scriptureSecondaryQuote":"And that he was buried, and that he rose again the third day according to the scriptures.","scriptureAfterSecondary":"The gospel is news.\n\nChrist died.\nChrist was buried.\nChrist rose again.","scriptureSupplementBlocks":[{"type":"scripture","reference":"Romans 3:24","quote":"Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"Ephesians 2:8-9","quote":"For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Not of works, lest any man should boast."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"Ephesians 2:10","quote":"For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works."}],"teachingPoints":["1. The gospel is good news\n\nPaul summarizes the gospel by pointing to what Jesus has done.\n\nChrist died.\nChrist was buried.\nChrist rose again.\n\nThat is news.\n\nThe gospel is not first a command to repair yourself.\n\nIt is the announcement that God has acted in Christ to save sinners.","2. Salvation is received, not earned\n\nEphesians says we are saved by grace through faith.\n\nNot by works.\n\nNot by spiritual performance.\n\nNot by proving we are good enough.\n\nSalvation is a gift.\n\nFaith receives what grace provides.","3. Grace comes before good works\n\nEphesians 2:10 says believers are created in Christ Jesus unto good works.\n\nThat order matters.\n\nWe are not saved by good works.\n\nWe are saved for good works.\n\nGrace does not leave us unchanged, but change begins after receiving Christ, not before.","4. Jesus moves the focus away from self\n\nEvery self-salvation system puts the weight on us.\n\nThe gospel puts the focus on Jesus.\n\nHis life.\nHis death.\nHis resurrection.\nHis grace.\nHis finished work.\n\nThe Christian life begins by looking away from self and trusting Christ."],"wordStudyBeforeStudyInsight":true,"wordStudyStepTitle":"Word Insight","wordStudyStepIntro":"","wordStudy":{"surface":"Gospel","lemma":"εὐαγγέλιον","transliteration":"euangelion","meaning":"Good news.","strongs":"G2098","reference":"1 Corinthians 15:1","note":"The gospel is not good advice about how to save yourself.\n\nIt is good news about what God has already done in Jesus.\n\nAdvice points to what you must accomplish.\n\nThe gospel points to what Christ has accomplished for you."},"studyInsight":{"title":"Study Insight","placement":"after_teaching","variant":"christ_connection","body":"The difference between advice and news is huge.\n\nAdvice says:\n\"Here is what you need to do.\"\n\nNews says:\n\"Here is what has already happened.\"\n\nThe gospel is news before it becomes instruction.\n\nJesus has already entered humanity.\nJesus has already lived the faithful life.\nJesus has already died for our sins.\nJesus has already risen from the dead.\nJesus has already opened the way to God.\n\nFaith does not create those facts.\n\nFaith receives them.\n\nThat is why Christian transformation begins with trust, not striving.\n\nWe do not obey to make God love us.\n\nWe begin to obey because His love has already reached us in Christ."},"studyInsightBlocks":[{"type":"studyVisual","title":"Advice or news?","accent":"stone","payload":{"variant":"comparison","leftTitle":"Good advice","rightTitle":"Good news","leftItems":["Try harder to become accepted"],"rightItems":["Jesus has acted to save you by grace"]},"footnote":"The gospel begins with what Christ has done."},{"type":"scriptureChain","title":"The Gospel Is Good News","references":[{"reference":"1 Corinthians 15:1-4"},{"reference":"Romans 3:24"},{"reference":"Ephesians 2:8-10"},{"reference":"Titus 3:5"}]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Takeaway: The gospel announces what Jesus has already done. We receive salvation by grace through faith, and good works flow from that new life."}],"reflectPrompt":"Where are you most tempted to treat Christianity like self-improvement instead of good news?\n\nThink about guilt, performance, trying to earn God's approval, or feeling like you need to become better before coming to Jesus.","lifeApplicationStepTitle":"Life Application and Prayer","lifeApplication":"This week, pay attention to the voice you are living under.\n\nDoes it sound like this?\n\n\"Do more so God will accept you.\"\n\nOr does it sound like this?\n\n\"Receive what Jesus has done, then walk with Him.\"\n\nWhen guilt pushes you into striving, return to the gospel:\n\nChrist died for my sins.\nChrist rose again.\nSalvation is a gift.\nGood works flow from grace.\n\nDo not start with yourself.\n\nStart with Jesus.\n\nPrayer:\n\nFather, thank You that the gospel is good news, not a command to save myself. Thank You for what Jesus has already done through His life, death, and resurrection. Help me receive Your grace by faith. Free me from striving for acceptance, and teach me to live from the salvation I have in Christ. Amen.","prayer":"","completionSummary":"The gospel is good news, not good advice. Salvation begins with what Jesus has already done, and the new life flows from receiving His grace by faith.","lessonQuiz":{"eyebrow":"CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING","title":"Quick Review","description":"Check your understanding before moving on.","settings":{"quizRequired":false,"passingScore":70,"allowRetake":true},"questions":[{"id":"mnic-l1-q1","prompt":"According to 1 Corinthians 15:3-4, what are central facts of the gospel?","options":["Christ died for our sins, was buried, and rose again","Humans must save themselves","Good advice is enough","Sin does not matter"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Paul summarizes the gospel by pointing to Christ's death for our sins, His burial, and His resurrection."},{"id":"mnic-l1-q2","prompt":"According to Ephesians 2:8-9, how are we saved?","options":["By grace through faith","By works alone","By being naturally perfect","By comparing ourselves to others"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Ephesians says we are saved by grace through faith, and that salvation is the gift of God."},{"id":"mnic-l1-q3","prompt":"What role do good works play according to Ephesians 2:10?","options":["They flow from being created in Christ Jesus","They earn God's love","They replace faith","They make grace unnecessary"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Ephesians 2:10 says believers are created in Christ Jesus unto good works. Good works are the fruit of salvation, not the root."},{"id":"mnic-l1-q4","prompt":"What is the main difference between advice and news in this lesson?","options":["Advice tells what must be done, news announces what has been done","Advice is always biblical and news is not","News tells people to save themselves","Advice is the same thing as grace"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"The lesson explains that advice gives instructions, while news announces an accomplished reality. The gospel announces what Christ has done."},{"id":"mnic-l1-q5","kind":"reflection","prompt":"What would change if you started your faith with what Jesus has done instead of what you need to prove?","explanation":"The gospel moves the focus from self-salvation to Christ's finished work, freeing us to live from grace instead of striving."}]}}
$mnic_l1_reader$::jsonb
where slug = 'good-news-not-good-advice'
  and study_series_id = 'e4000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000079';

-- Made New in Christ — Lesson 2: What Jesus Already Finished (guided reader JSON).
