-- When Death Died — Lesson 5: The Power of Death Broken (guided reader JSON).
delete from public.lesson_sections
where lesson_id = 'd3000007-0000-4000-8000-000000000884';

update public.lessons
set reader_content = $wdd_l5_reader$
{"openingThought":"Death has ruled the human story like an enemy no one could escape.\n\nEvery generation has faced it.\nEvery family has felt it.\nEvery heart has feared it.\n\nBut Jesus stepped into death and broke its power from the inside.\n\nHe did not merely survive death.\n\nHe conquered it.\n\nThrough His death and resurrection, Jesus destroyed the enemy's hold and freed humanity from the fear that death gets the final word.\n\nThe grave is still real.\n\nBut because of Jesus, it is no longer final.","scriptureRef":"Hebrews 2:14","scriptureQuote":"That through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil.","scriptureAfterPrimary":"This sounds strange at first.\n\nBut this is the wisdom of God.\n\nJesus did not defeat death by avoiding it.\n\nHe defeated death by entering it, carrying sin's weight, remaining faithful, and rising victorious.","scriptureSecondaryRef":"Hebrews 2:15","scriptureSecondaryQuote":"And deliver them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage.","scriptureAfterSecondary":"Death does not only affect the end of life.\n\nIt can shape how people live now.\n\nJesus came to free us from that bondage.","scriptureSupplementBlocks":[{"type":"scripture","reference":"2 Timothy 1:10","quote":"But is now made manifest by the appearing of our Saviour Jesus Christ, who hath abolished death, and hath brought life and immortality to light through the gospel."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"Revelation 1:18","quote":"I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore."},{"type":"scripture","reference":"1 Corinthians 15:26","quote":"The last enemy that shall be destroyed is death."}],"teachingPoints":["1. Jesus defeated death by entering it\n\nHebrews says Jesus destroyed the power of death through death.\n\nThe enemy used death as a weapon.\n\nJesus turned death into the place of victory.\n\nHe did not defeat death by avoiding it.\n\nHe defeated death by entering it, carrying sin's weight, remaining faithful, and rising victorious.","2. Death is connected to bondage\n\nHebrews 2 says people are held in bondage through the fear of death.\n\nDeath does not only affect the end of life.\n\nIt can shape how people live now.\n\nFear of death can produce anxiety, hopelessness, selfishness, despair, and spiritual slavery.\n\nJesus came to free us from that bondage.","3. Jesus brought life and immortality to light\n\n2 Timothy 1:10 says Jesus abolished death and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel.\n\nThat means the gospel gives us a clearer hope than human optimism ever could.\n\nLife is not found in pretending death is small.\n\nLife is found in knowing Christ has defeated it.\n\nJesus reveals that death is not stronger than God's saving love.","4. Jesus holds authority over death\n\nIn Revelation 1:18, Jesus declares that He was dead and is alive forevermore.\n\nThis is resurrection authority.\n\nThe One who passed through death now stands alive forever.\n\nDeath no longer speaks the final word.\n\nJesus does."],"wordStudyBeforeStudyInsight":true,"wordStudyStepTitle":"Word Insight","wordStudyStepIntro":"","wordStudy":{"surface":"Destroy","lemma":"καταργέω","transliteration":"katargeō","meaning":"To render powerless, break the hold of, or bring to nothing.","strongs":"G2673","reference":"Hebrews 2:14","note":"When Hebrews says Jesus destroyed the one who had the power of death, it means Christ broke the enemy's hold.\n\nThe devil still works through fear, deception, and death, but his final power has been defeated by the risen Christ."},"studyInsight":{"title":"Study Insight","placement":"after_teaching","variant":"christ_connection","body":"The resurrection changes how we understand death.\n\nWithout Jesus, death looks like the final wall.\n\nWith Jesus, death becomes a defeated enemy waiting for its final removal.\n\nThe Bible still calls death an enemy.\n\nIt does not ask us to pretend death is good.\n\nBut it also tells us that death has been broken by Christ and will one day be destroyed completely.\n\nThat means Christians do not grieve like people without hope.\n\nWe still feel loss.\nWe still cry.\nWe still hate what death has done.\n\nBut we do not bow to death as ultimate.\n\nJesus has already entered the grave and come out alive."},"studyInsightBlocks":[{"type":"studyVisual","title":"Death is real, but not final","accent":"sage","payload":{"variant":"comparison","leftTitle":"Death's power","rightTitle":"Christ's victory","leftItems":["fear","bondage","separation","grief"],"rightItems":["life","freedom","hope","resurrection"]},"footnote":"Death is real, but it is no longer final."},{"type":"scriptureChain","title":"Death's Power Broken","references":[{"reference":"Hebrews 2:14-15"},{"reference":"2 Timothy 1:10"},{"reference":"Revelation 1:18"},{"reference":"1 Corinthians 15:26"}]},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Takeaway: Jesus broke the power of death, freed humanity from fear, and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel."}],"reflectPrompt":"Where has the fear of death, loss, or uncertainty shaped the way you live?\n\nThink about anxiety, control, avoidance, hopelessness, grief, or the pressure to hold everything together.","lifeApplicationStepTitle":"Life Application and Prayer","lifeApplication":"This week, name one fear that death has attached itself to.\n\nIt may sound like:\n\n\"What if I lose someone?\"\n\"What if my life does not matter?\"\n\"What if everything ends in pain?\"\n\"What if I am not safe?\"\n\nThen bring that fear to Jesus.\n\nDo not pretend it is small.\n\nPlace it under the truth of the resurrection.\n\nSay:\n\n\"Jesus, You were dead, and You are alive forevermore.\"\n\nThe fear may not vanish instantly.\n\nBut it no longer gets to rule unquestioned.\n\nPrayer:\n\nJesus, thank You for entering death and breaking its power. Thank You that the grave could not hold You and that fear does not have to rule my life. Help me trust Your resurrection more deeply. Free me from bondage, strengthen my hope, and teach me to live in the light of Your victory. Amen.","prayer":"","completionSummary":"Jesus broke the power of death and freed humanity from fear. Because He lives forevermore, death is real, but it is no longer final.","lessonQuiz":{"eyebrow":"CHECK YOUR UNDERSTANDING","title":"Quick Review","description":"Check your understanding before moving on.","settings":{"quizRequired":false,"passingScore":70,"allowRetake":true},"questions":[{"id":"wdd-l5-q1","prompt":"According to Hebrews 2:14, what did Jesus destroy through death?","options":["Him that had the power of death, the devil","God's love","The need for faith","The value of human life"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Hebrews 2:14 says Jesus destroyed him that had the power of death, that is, the devil."},{"id":"wdd-l5-q2","prompt":"According to Hebrews 2:15, what were people delivered from?","options":["Bondage through fear of death","The promise of resurrection","The love of God","The hope of salvation"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Hebrews 2:15 says Jesus delivers those who were held in bondage through fear of death."},{"id":"wdd-l5-q3","prompt":"According to 2 Timothy 1:10, what did Jesus bring to light through the gospel?","options":["Life and immortality","Confusion and fear","Sin and condemnation only","Human pride"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"2 Timothy 1:10 says Jesus brought life and immortality to light through the gospel."},{"id":"wdd-l5-q4","prompt":"What does Jesus declare in Revelation 1:18?","options":["He lives, was dead, and is alive forevermore","Death defeated Him forever","The grave is stronger than God","Hope is impossible"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Revelation 1:18 shows Jesus' resurrection authority. He was dead, but He is alive forevermore."},{"id":"wdd-l5-q5","kind":"reflection","prompt":"How can the resurrection of Jesus challenge the fear that death has the final word?","explanation":"Jesus entered death and rose victorious. Death is still an enemy, but it is a defeated enemy because of Christ."}]}}
